.page passwd 5 the user database

# DESCRIPTION
`/Hakurei/etc/passwd` lists the users, one per line, in seven fields separated by colons:

    name:password:uid:gid:gecos:home:shell

The password field holds `x`: the real (hashed) passwords are in shadow(5), which only root can read. The gecos field is the full name. The shell is started by login(1), su(1) and init(8).

The shipped file:

    root:x:0:0:Yukari Yakumo:/root:/bin/gapsh
    reimu:x:1000:1000:Reimu Hakurei:/HumanVillage/reimu:/bin/gapsh
    marisa:x:1001:1001:Marisa Kirisame:/HumanVillage/marisa:/bin/gapsh
    sakuya:x:1002:1002:Sakuya Izayoi:/HumanVillage/sakuya:/bin/gapsh
    sumireko:x:1003:1003:Sumireko Usami:/HumanVillage/sumireko:/bin/gapsh

Accounts from uid 1000 up with a real shell appear on the login screen, if they have a seat (see group(5)). `adduser` and `deluser` edit this file; the tools that show names for numbers (`ls -l`, `id`, `ps`, `stat`) read it when they run, and gapsh reads it for `~user`.

# SEE ALSO
shadow(5), group(5), adduser(8), passwd(1), id(1), accounts(7)
